{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSZcDTEmo7jyfSpfMhGi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The rule keeps only the registers a sub-property needs and abstracts the rest. Rules that are not yet certain are marked \"Risk\" below. Refinement can repair them, though if the counterexamples point at the wrong choices it can run out of attempts.\n\n**Units**\n- The CSR register file and the data cache are cut. For ADDI they only matter for other instructions.\n  - Risk: if the cut CSR file can fire a trap that stops the write, refinement has to bring it back.\n- The instruction cache is cut, except when the sub-property compares `pc`. Then it is kept, because `RTL.near_mem$imem_pc` probably comes from it.\n\n**Registers**\n\n| Sub-property | Kept (`keep`) | `word` | `havoc` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `xk.frame` (rd!=k) | x_k, so its start value equals the RTL value | – | all others |\n| `xk.rs1=j` (rd==k) | x_j, and x0 when j=0 | x_k if k≠j | all others |\n| `mem` | x0 (it is compared) | – | all others |\n| `pc.rs1=a.rs2=b` (branches, stores) | x_a, x_b | – | all others |\n\n- **Frame:** x_k only has to stay unchanged when rd!=k, so it needs its start value.\n- **`word` for x_k:** the start value of x_k does not matter, because x_k gets overwritten. It still needs the RTL word and the ILA state, which are compared at the end.\n  - Risk: if the start and the end of the instruction can fall in the same cycle, the start value of x_k does matter.\n- **`mem`, when registers matter:** keep every register if the sub-property compares states other than `pc`, `load_en`, `store_en` and x0, such as load addresses. Also keep them all if the instruction is JALR, where `pc` depends on rs1. Otherwise refinement would have to restore up to 31 registers one at a time, which is more than 10 attempts.\n  - JALR is detected by a whole-token match on the description, which is not a structured field.\n\n**Operators**\n- All are kept. Replacing them changes no state bits, because adders are combinational.\n- A 32-bit add is cheap for the model checker.\n- Picking the wrong RTL pairing, such as the load address adder instead of the ALU result, would only add a spurious counterexample.\n\n```python\ndef tokens_of(text):\n    toks = []\n    cur = \"\"\n    for ch in text:\n        if ch.isdigit() or ch.lower() != ch.upper() or ch == \"_\":\n            cur = cur + ch\n        else:\n            if cur:\n                toks.append(cur)\n            cur = \"\"\n    if cur:\n        toks.append(cur)\n    return toks\n\n\ndef state_reg(s):\n    if s.startswith(\"x\") and len(s) > 1 and s[1:].isdigit():\n        return int(s[1:])\n    return None\n\n\ndef last_inst_token(inst):\n    parts = inst.split(\".\")\n    return parts[len(parts) - 1]\n\n\ndef choose(sub, design):\n    choices = design.get(\"choices\", [])\n    states = sub.get(\"states\", []) or []\n    terms = sub.get(\"case_terms\", []) or []\n    operand_fields = design.get(\"operand_fields\", []) or []\n    desc_toks = set([t.upper() for t in tokens_of(design.get(\"description\", \"\") or \"\")])\n\n    rd_eq = None\n    rd_ne = None\n    field_vals = {}\n    for t in terms:\n        f = t.get(\"field\")\n        op = t.get(\"op\")\n        v = t.get(\"value\")\n        if f == \"rd\":\n            if op == \"==\":\n                rd_eq = v\n            else:\n                rd_ne = v\n        elif op == \"==\":\n            field_vals[f] = v\n\n    reg_states = [state_reg(s) for s in states if state_reg(s) is not None]\n    other_states = [s for s in states if state_reg(s) is None]\n\n    keep_regs = set()\n    word_regs = set()\n    keep_all = False\n\n    if rd_ne is not None:\n        # frame: register must keep its value\n        keep_regs.add(rd_ne)\n    elif rd_eq is not None:\n        for f in operand_fields:\n            if f in field_vals:\n                keep_regs.add(field_vals[f])\n            else:\n                keep_all = True\n        if rd_eq not in keep_regs:\n            word_regs.add(rd_eq)\n    else:\n        # no rd in case: mem sub or branch/store per-state subs\n        for r in reg_states:\n            keep_regs.add(r)\n        if len(terms) == 0 and len(operand_fields) > 0:\n            basic = set([\"pc\", \"load_en\", \"store_en\"])\n            extra = [s for s in other_states if s not in basic]\n            if len(extra) > 0 or \"JALR\" in desc_toks:\n                keep_all = True\n        else:\n            for f in operand_fields:\n                if f in field_vals:\n                    keep_regs.add(field_vals[f])\n                else:\n                    keep_all = True\n\n    compares_pc = \"pc\" in states\n\n    out = {}\n    for c in choices:\n        cid = c[\"id\"]\n        kind = c.get(\"kind\")\n        levels = c.get(\"levels\", [])\n        lvl = levels[0] if levels else \"keep\"\n        if kind == \"unit\":\n            tok = last_inst_token(c.get(\"instance\", \"\"))\n            if tok == \"icache\" and compares_pc:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n            elif \"cut\" in levels:\n                lvl = \"cut\"\n            else:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n        elif kind == \"gpr\":\n            r = c.get(\"register\")\n            if keep_all or r in keep_regs:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n            elif r in word_regs:\n                lvl = \"word\" if \"word\" in levels else \"keep\"\n            else:\n                lvl = \"havoc\" if \"havoc\" in levels else (\"word\" if \"word\" in levels else \"keep\")\n        elif kind == \"operator\":\n            lvl = \"keep\"\n        if lvl not in levels and len(levels) > 0:\n            lvl = levels[0]\n        out[cid] = lvl\n    return out\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":24607,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephem